  "steps": [
    "Preheat oven to 275°F.",
    "Remove the thin membrane from the back of the rack (slide a knife under it, then peel off with your fingers; use a kitchen towel if slippery).",
    "Season both sides of ribs generously with salt and pepper.",
    "Place ribs meatiest-side down in a roasting pan or rimmed baking sheet. Cut in half if needed to fit.",
    "Cover tightly with foil (or wrap racks individually in foil packets).",
    "Bake 2.5 to 3.5 hours until meat falls easily from the bone. Check at 2 hours. Test with a knife: no resistance = done.",
    "While ribs bake, make the sauce: heat oil over medium, cook onion 5-8 min until soft. Add cumin, cook 30 sec. Add remaining sauce ingredients, stir, season with salt, cook 2 min. Set aside.",
    "Remove ribs from oven, discard foil, brush both sides with BBQ sauce.",
    "Move rack near top of oven, broil on high 3-4 min until sauce caramelizes. Watch closely."
